    @section qore_2_0_0 Qore 2.0.0

    @par Release Summary
    Major release of %Qore; see below for more information

    @subsection qore_2_0_0_new_features New Features in Qore
    - Improved Static Method resolution\n
      Static methods no longer need to be prefixed with the class name when called from other static methods; %Qore
      now resolves static methods in a manner similar to other programming languages based on the context of the call
    - New Modules
      - @ref asyncsocketiointro "AsyncSocketIo"
      - @ref discorddataproviderintro "DiscordDataProvider"
      - @ref discordrestclientintro "DiscordRestClient"
      - @ref discordwebsocketclientintro "DiscordWebSocketClient"
      - @ref gmaildataproviderintro "GmailDataProvider"
      - @ref googlecalendardataproviderintro "GoogleCalendarDataProvider"
      - @ref googledataproviderintro "GoogleDataProvider"
      - @ref logger_binintro "logger_bin"module
      - @ref mewsrestclientintro "MewsRestClient"
      - @ref mewsrestdataproviderintro "MewsRestDataProvider"
      - @ref netsuiterestclientintro "NetSuiteRestClient"
      - @ref openaidataproviderintro "OpenAiDataProvider"
      - @ref openairestclientintro "OpenAiRestClient"
      - @ref pop3clientdataproviderintro "Pop3ClientDataProvider"
      - @ref serversenteventclientintro "ServerSentEventClient"
      - @ref serversenteventhandlerintro "ServerSentEventHandler"
    - Module Updates
      - @ref dataproviderintro "DataProvider" module
        - added support for a data provider action catalog
          (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4808">issue 4808</a>)
      - @ref httpserverutilintro "HttpServerUtil" module
        - added support for CA cert locations to work around an openssl bug where the CA cert was not available in
          server sockets even though it was in the original cert file
          (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4915">issue 4915</a>)
      - @ref loggerintro "Logger" module
        - much faster faster execution with optimized code in the
          @ref logger_binintro "logger_bin" module
        - added a reopen event for rotatable appenders
      - @ref restclientintro "RestClient" module
        - implemented PKCE options for OAuth2 flows
          (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4820">issue 4820</a>)
    - New Methods
      - @ref Qore::FtpClient::isConnected() "FtpClient::isConnected()"
      - @ref Qore::HTTPClient::clearPersistent() "HTTPClient::clearPersistent()"
      - @ref Qore::HTTPClient::getHttpConfig() "HTTPClient::getHttpConfig()"
      - @ref Qore::HTTPClient::getPersistentCount() "HTTPClient::getPersistentCount()"
      - @ref Qore::HTTPClient::isPersistent() "HTTPClient::isPersistent()"
      - @ref Qore::Program::getCallerCapabilityMask() "Program::getCallerCapabilityMask()"
      - @ref Qore::Program::getCapabilityMask() "Program::getCapabilityMask()" normal and static methods
      - @ref Qore::Program::issueModuleCmd() "Program::issueModuleCmd()" static method
      - @ref Qore::Socket::startPollRecvData() "Socket::startPollRecvData()"
    - New Functions
      - @ref Qore::active_exception() "active_exception()"
      - @ref Qore::get_epoch_microseconds() "get_epoch_microseconds()"
      - @ref Qore::get_epoch_milliseconds() "get_epoch_milliseconds()"
    - Updated Functions
      - @ref Qore::parse_url() "parse_url()" supports @ref Qore::QURL_MAINTAIN_CASE "QURL_MAINTAIN_CASE"
    - New Date-Time Output Format Code
      - \c "@" was added as a @ref date_formatting "date/time output format code"
    - New Pseudo-Methods
      - @ref <callref>::uniqueHash() "<callref>::uniqueHash()"
      - @ref <date>::getEpochMicroseconds() "<date>::getEpochMicroseconds()"
      - @ref <date>::getEpochMilliseconds() "<date>::getEpochMilliseconds()"
      - @ref <string>::contains() "<string>::contains()"
      - @ref <string>::endsWith() "<string>::endsWith()"
      - @ref <string>::startsWith() "<string>::startsWith()"
    - New options supported in the @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient" class and subclasses:
      - \c username
      - \c password
    - The thousands separator can be suppressed in number formatting using the special character <tt>?</tt> in
      - @ref <float>::format() "<float>::format()"
      - @ref <int>::format() "<int>::format()"
      - @ref <number>::format() "<number>::format()"
      - @ref Qore::format_number(string, softfloat) "format_number(string, softfloat)"
    - Types can now return hashes with simple types for accept and returning types for compatibility reasons
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4876">issue 4876</a>)
    - Reflection is now allowed in module initialization and deletion closures

    @subsection qore_2_0_compatibility Fixes That Can Affect Backwards-Compatibility
    - @ref dataproviderintro "DataProvider" module
      - the \c AbstractDataProviderType::getAcceptTypeHash(*bool) and
        \c AbstractDataProviderType::getReturnTypeHash(*bool) abstract methods now take an optional argument; classes
        inheriting this class and reimplementing these methods must add the argument and the logic to respect it
    - fixed the list range operator to no longer return @ref NOTHING values for out of range elements
      - implemented the following parse options:
        - @ref broken-list-range "%broken-list-range"
        - @ref correct-list-range "%correct-list-range"
      - implemented the following new constant:
        - @ref Qore::PO_BROKEN_LIST_RANGE "PO_BROKEN_LIST_RANGE"
    - Subtracting @ref NOTHING from any value will result in the same value; previously this would result in
      @ref NOTHING

    @subsection qore_2_0_0_bug_fixes Bug Fixes in Qore
    - @ref bulksqlutilintro "BulkSqlUtil" module
      - fixed a bug executing bulk upsert operations with constant data
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4902">issue 4902</a>)
    - @ref connectionproviderintro "ConnectionProvider" module
      - fixed a bug where the I/O thread could stall and no longer ping any connection
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4896">issue 4896</a>)
      - fixed a bug where control characters in URLs were silently accepted
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4866">issue 4866</a>)
    - @ref httpserverintro "HttpServer" module
      - fixed a deadlock due to lock starvation in the @ref httpserverintro "HttpServer" regarding reloading HTTP certificate info
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4887">issue 4887</a>)
      - fixed a bug where the HTTP server did not disconnect idle connections
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4878">issue 4878</a>)
    - @ref oraclesqlutilintro "OracleSqlUtil" module
      - fixed a bug in the IN operator
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4901">issue 4901</a>)
      - fixed space management on Oracle
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4897">issue 4897</a>)
    - @ref sqlutilintro "SqlUtil" module
      - eliminated locking from DML operations
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4886">issue 4886</a>)
      - fixed a bug where \c SqlUtil::AbstractTable::getDropAllConstraintsAndIndexesOnColumnSql() did not work on
        foreign constraints
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4875">issue 4875</a>)
    - @ref swaggerintro "Swagger" module
      - fixed validating Swagger schemas with objects that declare no properties
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4906">issue 4906</a>)
      - fixed JSON and YAML parsing from HTTP messages without charset=utf-8 in the headers
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4895">issue 4895</a>)
      - fixed a bug converting arguments to fit the Swagger schema to avoid spurious and very difficult to debug type
        errors
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4825">issue 4825</a>)
      - fixed a bug where any additionalProperties would cause all properties to be accepted
        (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4823">issue 4823</a>)
    - fixed a bug where %Qore could crash due to excess usage of pthread thread-local keys
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4927">issue 4927</a>)
    - fixed a bug where copy methods were passed the new object as an argument instead of the old object
    - fixed a bug where a \c RUNTIME-TYPE-ERROR exception could be raised with valid calls at runtime
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4920">issue 4920</a>)
    - fixed a bug calculating relative date/time values against absolute dates on macOS
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4919">issue 4919</a>)
    - fixed a bug where control characters were not percent-encoded by @ref Qore::encode_url() "encode_url()"
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4917">issue 4917</a>)
    - fixed a crash in @ref Qore::pow(number, number) when \a y was \c 0n
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4916">issue 4916</a>)
    - improved the weak assignment operator to allow weak references to hashes and list containers
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4909">issue 4909</a>)
    - fixed a bug in deterministic garbage collection with class copy() methods
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4905">issue 4905</a>)
    - fixed a bug where %Qore would raise recusive constant exceptions when parsing in cases where values were not in
      a reference loop
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4903">issue 4903</a>)
    - fixed a bug resolving static class variables that could cause spurious errors
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4894">issue 4894</a>)
    - allow the persistent flag to be cleared without disconnecting in the @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient" class
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4882">issue 4882</a>)
    - reconnect HTTP client objects if already connected and a send/receive operation immediately gets disconnected
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4879">issue 4879</a>)
    - fixed a bug with the @ref minus_equals_operator "-= operator" and lvalues with
      @ref hash_or_nothing_type "*hash" types
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4873">issue 4873</a>)
    - fixed a bug where outputting complex data structures with deleted objects would cause spurious exceptions
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4862">issue 4862</a>)
    - fixed a bug where sockets could be prematurely closed due to I/O timeouts in some cases
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4858">issue 4858</a>)
    - fixed a bug with the @ref cast "cast<>()" operator and compatible typed hashes
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4840">issue 4840</a>)
    - fixed a bug where a hash subtracted by @ref NOTHING resulted in @ref NOTHING instead of the same hash
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4834">issue 4834</a>)

